<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pōmare IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a>–<a href="/years/1877">1877</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Queen Pōmare</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pōmare IV was queen of Tahiti for fifty years, from 1827 to 1877. Her reign was dominated by rivalry between British Protestant missionaries and French Catholic priests, which led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to impose a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1842 and to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-tahitian-war">Franco-Tahitian War</a> of 1844–1847. She kept her throne under French protection, and her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-v">Pōmare V</a> ceded the kingdom in 1880.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pomare-iv.jpg" alt="Pōmare IV" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen_Pomare%27s_Palace,_Tahiti_(LMS_illustration).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
